    "notes": "1. The 'total_revenue' field is constructed from the three line items under 'Revenues and other income' as presented in the primary statement. 2. The 'total_operating_cost' field is constructed from all line items under 'Costs and other deductions' EXCEPT for 'Interest expense', as interest is a financing cost, not an operating cost. 'Other taxes and duties' are included as they are considered operating costs for an oil & gas company (e.g., production taxes, property taxes). 3. 'Net income' uses the line 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil' as the final, consolidated bottom-line figure. 4. 'Taxes' uses 'Income tax expense (benefit)'. 5. 'Interest expenses' uses the 'Interest expense' line item. 6. All values are taken directly from the primary income statement table. Supplementary tables provide detailed breakdowns (e.g., components of 'Other income', details of 'Depreciation and depletion', breakdown of 'Other taxes and duties' and 'Income tax expense') but these are not required for the normalized consolidated values per the schema. 7. The scale is 1E6 (millions) as indicated in the statement header. 8. Per rule 13, all values for taxes, interest_expenses, and total_operating_cost are reported as positive numbers as they reduce income.",
